  "question": {
    "text": "If the distance between planes, $4 x-2 y-4 z+1=$ 0 and $4 x-2 y-4 z+d=0$ is 7 , then $d$ is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "PadZW",
      "text": "\n41 or $-42$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tTf8O",
      "text": "\n42 or $-43$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6G3YN",
      "text": "\n$-41$ or 43\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Rhnix",
      "text": "\n$-42$ or 44",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given planes are\n$$\n4 x-2 y-4 z+1=0\n$$\nand $4 x-2 y-4 z+d=0$\nThey are parallel.\nDistance between them is $\\pm 7$\n$=\\frac{d-1}{\\sqrt{16+4+16}}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\Rightarrow \\frac{d-1}{6}=\\pm 7 \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow d=42+1 \\\\\n&\\text { or }-42+1 \\\\\n&\\text { i.e. } d=-41 \\text { or } 43 .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
